{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(not_rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (not rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square in the coordinate plane has vertices whose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinates are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of the square?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/894b896905865a3bd3383f8dde5873c53dd1adce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 16\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 17\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 25\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 26\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/7355fccf2232e40fd3babba9bc7034e256163adf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(180);  pair A=(0,0); pair B=(4,1); pair C=(3,5); pair D=(-1,4);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(1));  dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NW);  // axes draw((-2,0)--(5,0), Arrow); draw((0,-1)--(0,6), Arrow);  label(&quot;$x$&quot;, (5,0), E); label(&quot;$y$&quot;, (0,6), N); [/asy]\" width=\"302\" height=\"302\" />\n</p><p>~Diagram by apmathematician\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the points be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42ca4ba410a859a59c3e7716755a88b12154a592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(x_1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/0062922127d104a05c676f827762dbb234348ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(x_2,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0d9ee2e9a3d1011bcf3cb648f09494917d1729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(x_3,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e2b82f216341575eed8b9f922eb3f7a037cf2f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(x_4,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Note that the difference in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. By rotational symmetry of the square, the difference in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Note that the difference in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We now know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, the side length of the square, is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b5adecf8cf897ce89c441a7652b63f44cc1dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1^2+4^2}=\\sqrt{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" />, so the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/109b9adb81c91588c896f1ce3baf3d27e5a7744f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By translation, we can move the square with point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> at the origin. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c476f8e23af256a66bb89c928a1e51c72f13ca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(0,0), B=(x_1,1), C=(x_2,5), D=(x_3,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"20\" />. We will use the relationship among the 4 sides of being perpendicular and equal.\n</p><p>The slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c0295b022fc334cf911abf953264661b792b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-0}{x_1-0}=\\frac{1}{x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"101\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, the slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a844deca7f3bed84c4e125b099b117d6966934c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=-x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />.\nFrom the information above we could have the equation: \n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271258edfc5af3c5733bfd0764d95869e04a8055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5-1}{x_2-x_1}=-x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"120\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055c7437507495243710543409b9d31606c95d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x_1 \\cdot x_2+x_1^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a7df8cb20c45ed05bb97bec61f0b4f0bb32ca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\cdot x_2=x_1^2-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dec0c4a2eb06a4b64fcb624ae29e32efa788ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2=\\frac{x_1^2-4}{x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"97\" height=\"44\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, the slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9fe41de628052d9ea5e7cb48efad882435128c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=\\frac{1}{x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"78\" height=\"41\" />.\nFrom the information above we could have the equation: \n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72265f83a83935ed8a0b30a779941252c226cf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5-4}{x_2-x_3}=\\frac{1}{x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"110\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953d4cee0c8368abc1942777fdf5abb716c1131e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2-x_3=x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3d7ceb26dec5ed32249d6fa73e6910ce07d0d84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_1^2-4}{x_1}-x_3=x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"137\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c875303cbd324e168907bc91717e162ac5a6526d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2-4-x_1 \\cdot x_3 = x_1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/26072d9ed3a62bdab1be045395c4c74d3fecc1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\cdot x_3=-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/853675edec463fff55e005d97cc885f8850dffb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3=- \\frac{4}{x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"80\" height=\"41\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b77aa9d502ea9136e4d664bdb37251ee3d549dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=AB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/1605b4fb1247756c718551ffef46bfa7fcf094e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x_3^2 +4^2} = \\sqrt{x_1^2+1^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"24\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f51ed5dc6f7aae0f574d6a3dd5f1ef8e03882d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(- \\frac{4}{x_1})^2 +4^2} = \\sqrt{x_1^2+1^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"215\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2d1584c66116c1c3dee88613f143dd22a5a2e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{x_1^2}+16=x_1^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"138\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d887b9ffe2af94ace700a952c1e19fafc07b98c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{x_1^2}+15=x_1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"106\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b279c9924407438893f325369b56b18aca6d23e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16+15x_1^2=x_1^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c6394f58bcd516e2640b348dc8f597e279943e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Let$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/2/862b4fde3370f385f02e4af1fb1417e9b1c914f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x_1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9583af9bfa5d1acfc990c9e0afef192f417d27a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16+15y=y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee893e62cfce6323ced74a11d79d16e7795beb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-15y-16=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b76dc92a63ecd66d6aff0e83c2c9738b43c51bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y-16)(y+1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf709e521fe3f0bae584d735bda8a7c0b5627984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34db3f30b0ec56bcf0ed3e144a9ef30b4dfba5a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=\\pm4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Note that the square with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/8/198ae8d9108463fd045f2bdacbc7378dbd0c06a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" /> is just the reflection of square with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19832f3c5f67e0cc0c1d826febc1555c591d258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> over the origin. I will use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19832f3c5f67e0cc0c1d826febc1555c591d258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5abf1fae282c74368a27425cbcf32ccc7b5686b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(4,1), AB=\\sqrt{17}, [ABCD]=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"340\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this solution, we will use the fact that the diagonals of a square bisect each other, they are perpendicular to each other, and they are equal in length.\n</p><p>Using the fact that the diagonals bisect each other, we get the equation:\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/b/c2bafdd4c6ff1ddb2e353252135cef8513e47e45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x_2}{2}=\\frac{x_1+x_3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfea22b1d9d3ad8df5e0db88b423eb37ad8a825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2=x_1+x_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Now we use the fact that the diagonals are perpendicular to each other:\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547b4e7506586cd0d464482ddb0d4e1d2fb2a387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Slope$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ced6e765051af1dcd3d53fb96741c775b868d7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$of$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c2802ee37ac57485c93a2c02b37aead50dcbaa60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\frac{5-0}{x_2}=\\frac{5}{x_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"144\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547b4e7506586cd0d464482ddb0d4e1d2fb2a387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Slope$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ced6e765051af1dcd3d53fb96741c775b868d7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$of$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0b5f558e5ffef44a908131f567de8960e7ae0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=\\frac{4-1}{x_3-x_1}=\\frac{3}{x_3-x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"204\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5aabc21823be96c05920b653e042a1fab12977c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{x_2} \\cdot \\frac{3}{x_3-x_1} = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"146\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/03964770dcc66ec8234fc136d81153df7d5755b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2(x_1-x_3)=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Using the fact that the diagonals are equal in length, we get the equation:\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b3d02ba8ae33b01eb06042357b8e6fa089576ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=AC$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a911c6baeaacbac103bf163feab88f92e6c2e2d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4-1)^2+(x_3-x_1)^2=5^2+x_2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da274671c09f7cb159313d61279564e34480ec91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+(x_3-x_1)^2=25+x_2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9666a7b3935d92422f0722d6cf1d7e20f10f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_3-x_1)^2-x_2^2=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Now we have 3 equations with 3 variables:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53e219a5cb9765798c64521dec751b02dc26243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{cases} x_2=x_1+x_3 \\\\ x_2(x_1-x_3)=15 \\\\ (x_3-x_1)^2-x_2^2=16 \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -34px\" width=\"198\" height=\"77\" />\n</p><p>We substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> into the 2 other equations:\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc264e4ad1265b14968a259562e9fa6a09912113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1+x_3)(x_1-x_3)=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356a6a038d757ff192d572819ea5447b2310506c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2-x_3^2=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" />\n</pre>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4eb0b3942b53b08e4444c3275c55c13b08b9c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_3-x_1)^2-(x_3+x_1)^2=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5f336b70222f5a50a1d62e24b1682690130f36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3^2-2x_1x_3+x_3^2-x_1^2-2x_1x_3-x_3^2=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f7e901b214f73679508c27b028d2fabb883cb48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-4x_1x_3=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5ff17e913178dda181ca06e38e7757a612c7b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1x_3=-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Now we have 2 equations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee60922c5fc5ee1941df04f838cdae71fbc29d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed4765b60d2fd3882bac1bef8f018cb575650fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{cases} x_1^2-x_3^2=15 \\\\ x_1x_3=-4 \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"135\" height=\"55\" />\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/853675edec463fff55e005d97cc885f8850dffb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3=- \\frac{4}{x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"80\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/8/1e827296ebbd3304c7c364c9e11c5638cc1a240c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2-(- \\frac{4}{x_1})^2=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38b6364336ed5a8a4175c4f63ba35510f3219492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2- \\frac{16}{x_1^2}=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"106\" height=\"42\" />\n</pre>\n<p>This is the same equation as solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/2141041193e2a887cf0f01a826e336cf04e432ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1= \\pm 4, AB=\\sqrt{17}, [ABCD]=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"326\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28not_rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(not_rigorous)\">Solution 4 (not rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (not rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw it out, by inspection the coordinates are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9ba91b378b33b75a172e77e70e8396ff92f641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78561eb59286ee78766fdc37ef35399bf0355e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9492e0ae17ba8045ad2de885400cf91207e83db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4b50f1e36b272a95db1bb8507a23b6e3c0f08f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{17}, [ABCD]=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" />\n~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iPPQUrNE4RE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iPPQUrNE4RE</a>\n</p><p>~ naren_pr\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A\">2014 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.ph